  """Five subzones: Amandi (the warmest, on the Sil's sunny north bank near Sober, with the steepest terraces), Chantada (the Miño around Belesar, cooler), Quiroga-Bibei (the upper Sil and Bibei, warmer, drier, with slate and Mediterranean scrub), Ribeiras do Miño and Ribeiras do Sil. Soils are slate, schist and granite; summer heat in the canyons ripens Mencía well despite Galicia's rain.""",
